{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-e17c9a07-8eeb-4f35-a1b7-5e90d667abdb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8788faea4bc60443","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9013-c0x7ud7g/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-decomposition.md","content":"# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9013 (FIPS 140-3 compliance for the model serving stack)\n\n## Triage Outcome\n\nNot below-threshold: the strategy spans two components (KServe, Platform Operator),\nmultiple distinct work streams (image remediation, CI enforcement, compliance\nevidence assembly and external submission, documentation), and a large share of\nthe schedule is dominated by external/human gates (accredited laboratory\ncertification with six-to-nine month turnaround, mandatory security review board\nsign-off) that are not AI-implementable. Not docs-only: code and image changes\nare required. Full decomposition follows.\n\n## Epic List\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Team | Component | Priority |\n|----|-------|------|------|-----------|----------|\n| RHAISTRAT-9013-E001 | FIPS crypto module inventory for serving-stack images | Implementation | RHOAI Serving | KServe | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9013-E002 | Remediate KServe and serving data plane images to validated crypto modules | Implementation | RHOAI Serving | KServe | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9013-E003 | Remediate Platform Operator image to validated crypto modules | Implementation | RHOAI Platform | Platform Operator | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9013-E004 | CI gating check for FIPS crypto regressions | Implementation | RHOAI Serving | KServe | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9013-E005 | Compliance evidence package assembly and submission to certification lab | Implementation | RHOAI Serving | KServe | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9013-E006 | Document FIPS support posture and cluster prerequisites | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Serving | Documentation | P0 |\n\n## Dependency