which modules are exercised in the inference request path versus\n50\t  ancillary paths (startup, metrics, tooling).\n51\t- Document the full inventory in a reviewable artifact suitable for inclusion\n52\t  in the compliance evidence package.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- Every serving-stack image is covered by the inventory; none are missing.\n57\t- Each crypto module carries a validated/non-validated classification with a\n58\t  citable source for the claim.\n59\t- The request-path versus ancillary-path distinction is recorded per module.\n60\t- The inventory artifact is complete enough that a third party can determine\n61\t  which images require remediation without re-deriving the analysis.\n62\t- The classification criteria are documented precisely enough to be encoded as\n63\t  a machine-readable allow/deny list for CI enforcement.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- HLR-2 (P0): the module inventory is an explicit component of the compliance\n68\t  evidence package.\n69\t- HLR-1 (P0): the inventory defines which images and modules block\n70\t  FIPS-enabled-cluster correctness.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5ebd1102387e562","agent_id":"afadad7e70f969e0e","session_id":"95f10158-af0c-4809-b17b-36c6f2e3eed3","uuid":"a66faf8e-cf78-42ad-a1e4-2dcb84f0625d","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:40:16.767Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfdf9184691f10bf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
