cceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- All KServe and serving data plane images run correctly on a FIPS-enabled\n54\t  OpenShift cluster: models deploy and serve inference requests successfully.\n55\t- No non-validated crypto library is linked in the inference request path of\n56\t  any serving image.\n57\t- Build attestations and test results for each remediated image are recorded\n58\t  and available as certification evidence.\n59\t- Any request-path dependency that cannot be remediated is explicitly\n60\t  documented with its blocking reason and owner.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-1 (P0): serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters\n65\t  using validated crypto modules.\n66\t- HLR-2 (P0, supporting): produces the build attestations and test results the\n67\t  evidence package requires.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5ebd1102387e562","agent_id":"afadad7e70f969e0e","session_id":"95f10158-af0c-4809-b17b-36c6f2e3eed3","uuid":"1929b473-46ca-4432-b918-882e93cd8ce2","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:40:17.555Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-96dcc08e910ab668","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
