rate all container images shipped by the serving stack (KServe\n51\t  components, serving data plane images, Platform Operator image).\n52\t- For each image, identify all linked cryptographic libraries and modules\n53\t  (direct and transitive), including base-image and language-runtime crypto.\n54\t- Classify each module as FIPS 140-3 validated or non-validated, citing the\n55\t  validation record where one exists.\n56\t- Record which modules are exercised in the inference request path versus\n57\t  ancillary paths (startup, metrics, tooling).\n58\t- Document the full inventory in a reviewable artifact suitable for inclusion\n59\t  in the compliance evidence package.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- Every serving-stack image is covered by the inventory; none are missing.\n64\t- Each crypto module carries a validated/non-validated classification with a\n65\t  citable source for the claim.\n66\t- The request-path versus ancillary-path distinction is recorded per module.\n67\t- The inventory artifact is complete enough that a third party can determine\n68\t  which images require remediation without re-deriving the analysis.\n69\t- The classification criteria are documented precisely enough to be encoded as\n70\t  a machine-readable allow/deny list for CI enforcement.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- HLR-2 (P0): the module inventory is an explicit component of the compliance\n75\t  evidence package.\n76\t- HLR-1 (P0): the inventory defines which images and modules block\n77\t  FIPS-enabled-cluster correctness.\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a78dfcbc2c3fb87","agent_id":"a752be556e5bc2e5f","session_id":"95f10158-af0c-4809-b17b-36c6f2e3eed3","uuid":"b01a0431-4888-49c3-90da-8b82258db740","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:49:08.330Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9229d5b614950df8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9